/* ===========================================================================
   cmapdata.js — the colormap tables themselves
   "How Colormaps Actually Work"
   Heather Bedle and April Moreno-Ward / AASPI / University of Oklahoma

   Each table is a run of six-character hex triplets at 256 levels (ten for the
   categorical map). These are the published definitions, not ramps rebuilt
   from a handful of anchor colors, because the whole subject of this module
   set is what happens between the anchors.

     Crameri, F., 2018, Scientific colour maps, doi:10.5281/zenodo.1243862
       — oslo, viridis's companions batlow and lajolla, roma, vik, romaO
     Thyng, K. M. et al., 2016, True colors of oceanography, Oceanography 29(3)
       — balance
     Smith, N. and van der Walt, S., 2015, https://bids.github.io/colormap
       — viridis
     Moreland, K., 2009, Diverging color maps for scientific visualization
       — coolwarm
     matplotlib — jet, rainbow, gist_rainbow, nipy_spectral, Spectral, bwr,
       seismic, RdYlGn, prism, afmhot, cool, turbo, hsv, gray, tab10

   The maps under era 'traditional' are here to be compared against, not
   because they are recommended. Several are long-standing defaults in
   interpretation practice and appear in published figures going back decades.
   bgyor, rainbowwc, legacy16, rwg, mwc, rg and rkb are reconstructions of
   arrangements in common use rather than copies of any one implementation.

   MEASURED FIELDS. These are computed from the table itself, not asserted:
     lmin, lmax   the CIE L* range the map covers
     lmono        1.0 if lightness runs one way from end to end, 0.0 if it
                  returns to where it started. Sequential maps should be 1.0.
     gmin, gmax   the smallest and largest local color difference along the
                  map, normalised so a perfectly uniform map is 1.0 throughout
     cvdmin       the same measure under the worst of protan, deutan and
                  tritan simulation. Values near zero mark a stretch of the
                  map that becomes one flat color.
   'uniform' and 'cvdSafe' are different: they record whether the map was
   designed for those properties, which is a fact about where it came from.
   =========================================================================== */

